        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.026,
            0.846,
            0.049
          ],
          "content": "Chapter 12 — How Nature Works in Harmony"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.888,
            0.029,
            0.923,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": "193"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.083,
            0.745,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "Each habitat has its own biotic components and physical conditions — air, sunlight, water, temperature, and soil. Different organisms living in the same habitat may use the resources in different ways. A forest might be warm during the day and cool at night. A snake that comes out at night and a rodent active during the day both live in the same habitat, but they face different conditions. This is how living organisms coexist in harmony in the same habitat."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.247,
            0.653,
            0.273
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "12.2 Who All Live Together in Nature?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.291,
            0.745,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": "You have observed fish in a pond in Activity 12.1. Did you see only a single fish? Most likely, you may have seen many fish of the same kind. This group of fish of the same kind living together in a pond habitat is called a **population** of that particular fish. In this way, we can observe and record populations of different kinds of organisms in a single habitat."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.419,
            0.484,
            0.443
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 12.2: Let us record"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.454,
            0.744,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "We can understand the population of a particular type of plant by counting them at a given place and time."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.495,
            0.547,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "Divide students into four to five groups."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.518,
            0.743,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": "Each group may identify any two organisms, plant(s) or animal(s)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.558,
            0.638,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "z Mark an area of 1 m × 1 m in your school garden."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.58,
            0.743,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": "z Identify four organisms in this area, and count their numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.602,
            0.65,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "z Record the number of the organisms in Table 12.2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.625,
            0.487,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "z Compile the data from all groups."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.655,
            0.805,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": "**Table 12.2: Number of partic**<strong><u>ular organisms at a given space</u></strong> **and time**"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.713,
            0.84,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "| Name of organism | Population (Number of individual organisms) |\n| --- | --- |\n| Plant 1: | 20 |\n| Plant 2 : | 05 |\n| Animal 1 : |  |\n| Animal 2 : |  |",
          "captions": [],
